  "description": "HAPROH crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C104 H214 Co6 O62 P6 Pr8. From the CIF bond table, Pr1 (Pr) has 11 O neighbors; Pr2 (Pr) has 7 O neighbors; Pr3 (Pr) has 7 O neighbors; Pr4 (Pr) has 8 O neighbors; Co1 (Co) has 6 O neighbors; Co2 (Co) has 5 O neighbors; Co3 (Co) has 6 O neighbors; Pr1A (Pr) has 11 O neighbors; Pr2A (Pr) has 7 O neighbors; Pr3A (Pr) has 7 O neighbors; Pr4A (Pr) has 8 O neighbors; Co1A (Co) has 6 O neighbors; Co2A (Co) has 5 O neighbors; Co3A (Co) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 22 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.186-4.008 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 81.94-119.52°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C104H214Co6O62P6Pr8.",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
